@*
    Carried over verbatim from the legacy <namespaces> list.

    Nop.Web.Framework is load-bearing for more than it looks: besides HtmlExtensions and
    LayoutExtensions it is where task 8.3 PROMOTED the @Html.Action(...) child-action
    bridge to (ChildActionExtensions, deferral 7.3-1). The namespace was chosen precisely
    so that this one already-present import picks it up and NO admin view call site had to
    change. Do not add Nop.Web.Extensions — that namespace no longer holds the bridge.
*@
@using Nop.Core.Events
@using Nop.Core.Infrastructure
@using Nop.Services.Events
@using Nop.Web.Framework
@using Nop.Web.Framework.Events
@using Nop.Web.Framework.Security.Captcha
@using Nop.Web.Framework.Security.Honeypot
@using Nop.Web.Framework.UI

@*
    Tag helpers. 3.90 had none (they do not exist in MVC 5), so nothing here is a port —
    these are added because the framework's own form/validation/link tag helpers are the
    supported way to get anti-forgery tokens emitted into forms, and Html.BeginForm relies
    on the same infrastructure. Same entry Nop.Web's _ViewImports.cshtml carries.
*@
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
